      "chunk_idx": 1,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## Background.",
      "token_count": 4,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A02:2025 Security Misconfiguration",
        "Background."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_0df66f6c3e23_c00002",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a02_security_misconfiguration",
      "version_id": "ver_0df66f6c3e23",
      "chunk_idx": 2,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "Moving up from #5 in the previous edition, 100% of the applications tested were found to have some form of misconfiguration, with an average incidence rate of 3.00%, and over 719k occurrences of a Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE) in this risk category.\n\nWith more shifts into highly configurable software, it's not surprising to see this category moving up.\n\nNotable CWEs included are *CWE-16 Configuration* and *CWE-611 Improper Restriction of XML External Entity Reference (XXE)*.",
      "token_count": 100,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A02:2025 Security Misconfiguration",
        "Background."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_0df66f6c3e23_c00003",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a02_security_misconfiguration",
      "version_id": "ver_0df66f6c3e23",
      "chunk_idx": 3,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
